Description: Neutralize broken dpkg-fast.patch LTO insertion inside compat-funcs list
Origin: PikaOS buildFixer (failure 76955)
Bug: https://git.pika-os.com/repo-tools/run-upstream-build/actions/runs/224469
Version: 1.23.8
Last-Update: 2026-09-08
 The previous dpkg-fast.patch revision (`@@ -215,0 +216,1 @@` adding
 `# Enable LTO for faster builds`) inserted a bare `#` comment inside the
 DPKG_CHECK_COMPAT_FUNCS([ ... ]) argument list (around scandir/alphasort).
 GNU m4 treats `#` as a comment, so the insertion truncates the continued
 list and leaves the opening `[` unterminated, producing
 `m4:configure.ac:204: ERROR: end of file in argument list` and failing
 `aclocal`/`autoreconf` in phase build (failure 76955, dpkg 1.23.8).
 LTO for the lto stage is supplied via build flags, not configure.ac edits,
 so replace the broken insertion with a no-op comment at top level that
 always applies.
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
 # Process this file with autoconf to produce a configure script.

+# PikaOS: neutralize broken dpkg-fast.patch LTO insert (failure 76955, dpkg 1.23.8); LTO via build flags.
 m4_pattern_forbid([^_?DPKG_])
